#24.2 — Primary Key Integrity

All 26 application tables had primary keys. hcgo_asset_scope correctly used the composite primary key (asset_id, scope_id), producing 27 PK-column rows across 26 tables. bta_testament uses the existing primary key name id; this was documented as an existing schema characteristic, not treated as a defect.

#24.3 — Foreign Key Integrity

Twenty-eight foreign-key relationships were returned and validated. Major relationship paths included:

BTA: bta_religion → bta_canon → bta_translation → bta_book → bta_chapter → bta_verse → bta_verse_text.
BTA/KAH bridge: bta_translation.asset_id → kah_asset.asset_id.
KAH/HCGO: kah_asset → hcgo_domain, hcgo_knowledge_type, hcgo_knowledge_role; asset governance through hcgo_asset_scope, hcgo_provenance, hcgo_ingestion_state and hcgo_publication_state; publication through kah_published_knowledge.
Domain-level capabilities: hcgo_domain → hcgo_domain_reference and hcgo_semantic_profile.

Observation retained for later architectural review: kah_asset.language_id and kah_asset.country_id exist without foreign-key constraints to ent_language and ent_country. No schema change was made during validation.

#24.4 — Unique Constraint Integrity

Twenty-five UNIQUE constraints were identified. Key examples:

bta_book: (translation_id, book_code)
bta_chapter: (book_id, chapter_number)
bta_verse: (chapter_id, verse_number)
bta_verse_text: (verse_id, translation_id)
hcgo_scope: (scope_type_id, scope_code)
hcgo_domain_reference: (domain_id, reference_url)
kah_asset: asset_code
kah_published_knowledge: (asset_id, reference_code)

No additional uniqueness was imposed on hcgo_provenance, hcgo_ingestion_state, or hcgo_publication_state because their current design may intentionally support multiple historical records per asset.

#24.5 — Nullability and Default Validation

The information_schema column inventory returned 195 application columns. Required identifiers/codes were generally NOT NULL, optional descriptive/metadata fields were nullable, boolean control fields used appropriate defaults, and HCGO timestamp fields used CURRENT_TIMESTAMP where designed.

A gap in kah_asset ordinal positions was investigated. PostgreSQL pg_attribute confirmed attnum 2 as '........pg.dropped.2........' with attisdropped = true. This proved the gap was normal PostgreSQL schema history caused by a previously dropped column, not a missing active column. No corrective action was required.

#24.6 — Identity / Sequence Integrity

Twenty-four automatically generated identifiers were identified. Earlier BTA/ENT/KAH structures use nextval()-backed PostgreSQL sequences, while newer HCGO structures predominantly use GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY. Both mechanisms were functioning as valid PostgreSQL identifier-generation patterns.

bta_testament.id and the hcgo_asset_scope composite key are intentionally supplied rather than automatically generated and therefore did not appear in the generated-identifier inventory.

#24.7 — Transactional Hub ↔ Spoke Relationship Validation

Behavioral testing was performed inside an explicit PostgreSQL transaction. The permanent BTAX domain (domain_id 1, Bible Therapy Assistant) was preserved and not used as disposable test data.

An initial invalid domain code TEST24 was intentionally rejected because hcgo_domain.domain_code is CHAR(4). The transaction was rolled back after the error, confirming enforcement of the domain-code length rule. A new transaction was then started with valid code T024.

